{
 "about": [
  "SB-3E A3/A4 data (design section 5; SB3E-R33.3). The tools read only this file for seams,",
  "binaries and controls; U4a-2 adds S3, S4b and S5 here, with their controls, without a scanner change.",
  "seams: each marker is the seam's `const M: &str` in `source`; no marker may be a substring of another.",
  "Per binary, 'reachable' means the marker survives a real release build with the cfg set (census);",
  "'unwired' proves nothing and rests on A5/A6. U17 and later may only move a seam to 'reachable'.",
  "ungates: exact edits removing a seam's cfg gates. controls: an ungate set plus a call on a path",
  "reachable from the binary's entry; a real link of that binary must report each `expect` seam.",
  "binaries: `shipped` names the script that installs the binary (A4 scans that binary), or null."
 ],
